[144.474812, "o", "201:def time_execution_with_cuda_event(\r\n202-    kernel_fn: callable,\r\n203-    args: list[Any],\r\n204-    num_warmup: int = 3,\r\n205-    num_trials: int = 10,\r\n206-    discard_first: int = 1, # set to 0 to disable\r\n207-    verbose: bool = True,\r\n208-    device: torch.device = None,\r\n209-) -> list[float]:\r\n210-    \"\"\"\r\n211-    Time a CUDA kernel function over multiple trials using torch.cuda.event\r\n212-    The first version of KernelBench used this for evaluation.\r\n213-    We care about cold cache performance here.\r\n214-\r\n215-    Note: this version does not guard against adverserial cuda streams yet.\r\n216-    It assumes computation is done on the current stream for current device. \r\n217-    Stay tuned for future PRs. \r\n218-\r\n219-    Args:\r\n220-        kernel_fn: Function to time\r\n221-        args: Arguments to pass to kernel_fn\r\n222-        num_warmup: Number of warmup iterations before timing\r\n223-        num_trials: Number of timing trials to run\r\n224-        discard_first: Number of first trials to discard, f"]
